iption":"Rig floor was very clean and organized. Crew was moving and communicating well with each other. Equipment was rigged up properly with no issues noted. ","location":"HP 479","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"78576262","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-04-05","observer":"Michael Hancock","type":"At-Risk Behavior","description":"While reaching over to grab a turbolizer to install in the casing, the crew members hand slid down to the threads on the casing putting his hand in a potential pinch point between the stump and the casing joint. ","location":"HP 479","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"78576261","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-04-05","observer":"Robert Keneson","type":"At-Risk Procedure","description":"After reliving the other side from the floor I got on the elevators and they felt off. I ran about 15 joints and shut down the job to inspect the elevators. After I inspected the elavtors I found that the safety latch wasn't holding correctly and elavtors were opening freely. We got the 2nd set to the floor and after I inspected those. It was the same outcome!","location":"Citadel 3","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"78575135","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-04-05","observer":"Robert Keneson","type":"At-Risk Behavior","description":"Thread rep ran under tongs. ","location":"Citadel 3 ","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"78574990","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-04-05","observer":"Robert Keneson","type":"At-Risk Procedure","description":"As I started running the elavtors after the other hands went down they felt off. After about 15 joints I shut the job down to inspect them. They safety latch was not working and they were opening freely. We sent them down and brought up the 2nd set and when I checked them. They didn't hold shut either. ","location":"Citadel 3","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"78574952","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-04-05","observer":"Michael Hancock","type":"At-Risk Behavior","description":"While operator was trying to push back the tongs, thread rep walked under tongs across the hydraulic cable to get to the casing to make his mark. ","location":"Citadel 3 ","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"78572971","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-04-05","observer":"Michael Hancock","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"After setting slips the elevators hit the collar clamp and it became loose and sat on top of the FMS. In inspection it was determined that two of the dies had come out. Driller was made aware and told the few to run the clamp with the missing dies. ","location":"Citadel 3 ","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"78572970","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-04-05","observer":"Antonio Acosta","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"While running casing. We were on landing joint and we had the swedge on. We noticed the diaper pin was damaged for the main pin on swedge ","location":"Gato grande 515h","service_line":"Drilling","report_number":"78572824","yard":""},{"date":"2026-04-05","observer":"Michael Gonzalez","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"While running casing on a small rig floor. The power tongs come within inches of elevators while the drillervis slacking off.","location":"Ensign T54","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"78572472","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-04-05","observer":"Michael Gonzalez","type":"Suggestion","description":"Questions about limitations were being asked about CRTi and CRTe. Some of which I didn't have an immediate answer for.","location":"H&P313 / casing","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"78572368","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-04-05","observer":"Shon Rodgers","type":"Recognition","description":"Our sse did a great safe job working the v door, he is picking it up quickly and retaining the information we're feeding him","location":"H&P 415.  Rig floor","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"78570742","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-04-05","observer":"Nicolas Lopez","type":"At-Risk Condition","descripti